WEBVTT

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.330
Today, the Hornets play against the Grizzlies.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:11.750
For their starting pitcher, the Hornets have brought out the attention-drawing rookie, Goro Shigeno!

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:16.630
He pitched against the Titans in his previous game and didn't give up a single run, pitching 100 mph left and right.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.840
He'll undoubtedly make the opening season roster.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.000
Now, what sort of pitching will he show us today?

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.410
It's decided.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:33.470
Your major league debut will be the third game of the season,

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:37.290
playing home against the Seattle Seagulls.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.830
You're fifth on the pitching rotation,

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:44.980
but the owner wanted your first game to be at home.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.600
Can you do it?

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:48.690
You bet.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.240
I'll give a flashy debut.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:59.910
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:59.910
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:05.210
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:05.210
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:10.590
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:10.590
the only thing I truly have

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:15.880
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:15.880
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:21.220
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:21.220
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:26.480
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:26.480
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.860
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.860
I had begun to understand many things

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:37.950
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:37.950
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:43.490
garakuta no yama kara

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:43.490
In the junk I've piled up,

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:47.580
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:47.580
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:52.880
hibike kono koe yo

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:52.880
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:59.140
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:59.140
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:04.810
namida kareru made

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:04.810
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:09.850
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:09.850
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:15.190
namida hareru made

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:15.190
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:20.200
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:20.200
though I may lose my way,

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.040
egakikake no ima

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.040
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.540
kizamu

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:31.290
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.830
akashi

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:31.290
kono te de

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.130
<b>Shimizu</b>

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:42.170
Good morning to everyone in Japan.

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:44.930
We are in Indianapolis, America,

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:49.850
to bring this to you from Brave Stadium, the home of the Indiana Hornets.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:53.710
The major league is divided into the Northern League and the Southern League,

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:59.000
and within each league, teams compete for first place in east, central, and west divisions.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.640
We're in the Northern League's central region.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:07.120
The Hornets are up against the Seagulls for their third game this season, and currently have one win and one loss.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.710
For this game, the Hornets have brought out the nineteen-year-old samurai

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:16.500
who drew everyone's attention at the World Cup and was brought up to the majors this spring.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:21.110
Shigeno Goro is making his major league debut!

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:24.960
What sort of pitching will he show us today?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.250
Honda...

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:34.230
A Prominent Debut!

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:34.230
A Prominent Debut!

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.670
Hey, Taiga!

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.200
The game's about to start!

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:45.160
You...

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.140
H-He's dead.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.960
This man approaching the batter's box, the first to face Shigeno,

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:57.250
is a major league superstar known for his consistent batting skills, Kyoshiro!

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.140
Play ball!

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.810
Are you watching, Dad?

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.230
This is the mound of the majors.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:17.150
I've been watching and playing baseball since I was born.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:21.690
At last, I've risen to the greatest stage

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:25.030
of the game you taught me, Dad!

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.620
Strike!

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:44.340
I've been through a lot, losing you, getting injured, and facing other challenges,

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:49.280
but thanks to Mom, my step-dad, the coaches,

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:53.910
and all my friends and rivals supporting me...

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:56.510
Strike!

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.940
I'm standing on this mound.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.810
He's fast.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:06.880
He's in a different league compared to how he pitched in the Japanese team training camp.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:12.540
But Dad, I'm not finished yet.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:18.850
You're only considered a real major leaguer when you've played well for three years.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.300
This is where the real battle starts as a professional player.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.720
I can't play Gibson anymore,

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:31.330
but next time I'll definitely strike him out!

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:35.770
And on this greatest stage,

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:39.690
I'll rise to the top!

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.370
Strike out!

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.490
He's smiling.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:55.250
Feeling relaxed in a major league game?

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.580
Let's see how long that lasts.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.000
Show us what you've got, super rookie.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.510
Excuse me.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.840
Master, would you like something to drink?

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:16.450
Coffee or wine, perhaps?

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:17.460
Right...

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:20.520
No, I can't have caffeine or alcohol.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.900
The doctor said I have to wait a little longer,

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.060
so I'll just have a glass of orange juice.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:26.470
Very well.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:29.320
Strike out!

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:36.750
In the top of the first inning, he struck out Kyoshiro, Gielen flied out, and the third batter also struck out.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:40.000
Shigeno's major league debut is off to a good start.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.710
Not a single hit from their entire lineup?

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:49.260
Not bad.

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:54.830
Shigeno, you won't make it!

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:55.990
Leave it to the third baseman!

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.390
What?

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:00.690
Out!

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:03.780
It's nothing to be surprised about.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:06.150
I only threw a ball.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:09.820
I was a righty before I broke my shoulder.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.730
Take a look at the excitement in the stands!

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:16.460
Very nice, Japanese boy.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.250
You're performing exactly as planned.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:24.670
I have a feeling that he'll become a star for the Hornets even though he just arrived.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:30.780
It's hard to imagine this is his major league debut seeing how calm he is.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.550
What a guy.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:36.990
Sanders, I heard you and him were a battery for the Bats.

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:38.690
Watts.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:39.880
Yeah.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:43.770
He was a closer back then, but you're our closer for the Hornets.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:46.910
Shigeno's young and he has stamina.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:49.360
He can do just as well as a starting pitcher.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.300
Yeah.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.910
I'd say that's best for him today.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:58.990
If he pitches first, he won't have to go through what he did in the World Cup final.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:05.170
The game has progressed well, with both teams being unable to score.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:08.590
Shigeno has shown us some fabulous pitching.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:14.970
Out!

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.310
Strike out!

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:23.770
Out!

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:30.360
Hey...

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.680
Shigeno hasn't given up a hit yet.

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.810
It's already the sixth inning.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.730
It might just keep going like this for a...

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.650
What are you saying?

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:44.020
You see this beginner's luck stuff all the time.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:47.370
It's through!

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:48.790
It's a hit! A hit!

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:51.460
The Hornets have a runner on and no outs!

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.630
Now, number six, Dunstan, is at bat.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:54.630
Come on.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:58.300
Will the Hornets be able to start the scoring?

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:58.300
Get a run somehow and support Honda.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.580
Bring the runner home, Dunstan!

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.440
A preemptive two runs!

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:15.490
That's to celebrate your major league debut.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:18.740
I couldn't ask for a better present, Dunstan.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:20.700
Ninety pitches after six innings.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:25.850
Shigeno has yet to give up a hit, and he comes back on the mound for the seventh inning.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:31.130
C-Could it possibly end up being a debut victory with...

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.800
...a no-hit game?

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:37.910
Even if he doesn't give up any hits this inning, don't tell Shigeno.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.550
No, I think he's already noticed.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.350
Strike out!

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:48.270
Just three at-bats again this inning...

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.510
Oh, man...

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:50.730
Are you serious?

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.260
This better be a joke.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:57.610
There's never been a pitcher in major league history who's debuted with a no-no game.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:00.900
Shigeno Goro... What a fearsome nineteen year-old!

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:04.280
In his first major league game, he's held down seven innings with no hits and no runs.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:07.710
Will he successfully set a record in major league history?

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:11.900
The entire stadium is shaking.

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:17.130
He's pitched 120 pitches so far, with twelve strike outs and one walk.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:21.430
And so far, he hasn't given up a hit on twenty-two batters!

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:24.060
Amazing!

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:25.830
Do you realize what you're doing?

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.260
Yeah, I sure do.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.980
I haven't given up a single hit, right?

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:33.650
Just six more outs.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:38.150
Your pitches are still strong, and it's an achievable goal if we continue like this.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:38.900
Yeah.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:42.320
Now that I've come this far, I'll definitely try to get there.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:47.620
Now hitting: number 29, Olerud!

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:50.080
Shigeno!

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:51.960
Stay focused, Shigeno!

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.170
Don't let us down.

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:57.210
To be honest...

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:02.300
I'm always shooting for a no-hitter until I give up my first hit of the game.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.970
This can't happen!

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:08.430
A rookie's no-hit debut would go down in history!

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:09.940
We must get a hit!

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:12.150
Get at least one hit, no matter what!

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:16.480
At this rate, I'll be the last batter.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:17.820
I don't like the sound of that.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.540
I-If he actually pitches a no-hitter...

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:25.570
With a record like that, we'll have more than just Japanese fans.

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:28.730
All of America will set their eyes on Shigeno.

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:31.160
Our profits will be huge this season...

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:37.500
Out!

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:40.420
Like hell I'll drop it.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.920
We're five outs away.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:44.850
Gameron enters the batter's box.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:50.040
He's grown again from the experience he gained at the World Cup.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.350
What a wonderful debut, Goro!

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:04.240
Safe!

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:19.320
First base was safe!

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:23.300
If it's a hit, this ends Shigeno's chance for a no-hitter debut.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.990
Was it a hit?

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:28.880
It's an error!

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:31.800
It was an error by the shortstop Roy!

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:35.620
Thank God...

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.230
Sorry about that.

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:41.760
Now hitting: number 32, Dean!

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:47.820
Strike!

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:49.110
All right.

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:51.500
He's still calm throwing from set position.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.750
Foul! Foul!

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:07.340
That must have scared Shigeno.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:11.010
The swing didn't connect very well, but the ball surprisingly flew.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.650
All right, we have him cornered.

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:15.270
No need to rush.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.870
Let's take this slowly.

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:24.320
Ball.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:25.820
Good.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.530
Keep that up.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:32.950
Oops.

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:37.180
The last time he was in this situation was at the World Cup.

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:40.790
Ball.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.340
What do you mean?

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:50.090
I'm saying that it's been a while since he's had to close a game with such a small score difference.

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:56.160
He was heavily padded in the two exhibition games and he only pitched for the first six innings.

00:13:56.970 --> 00:13:58.060
Ball!

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:02.090
It looks like he's getting tired.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:03.630
It's only a matter of time.

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:05.810
Go get someone warming up in the bullpen.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:06.730
Okay.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.980
Ball! Ball four!

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.690
What's he doing in this critical moment?

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.890
What's wrong all of a sudden?

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:26.100
Are you tired?

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:27.300
No.

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:30.970
It's not that I'm tired.

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:37.450
They're not going to take you out of a no-hitter.

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:41.240
If we let any more runners on base, they can turn the game around.

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:45.080
We shouldn't underestimate them, so pitch as hard as you can.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:46.040
Sure.

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:50.740
Now hitting: number 12, Wigginton!

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:53.950
One out, with runners on first and second

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:55.490
and a two-point lead.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:15:00.000
Shigeno has pitched a no-hitter so far, but now he's in trouble!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.740
Sanders, I'm going to warm up my shoulder.

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:03.820
Can you catch for me?

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:05.630
S-Sure.

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:11.950
Ball.

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:15.000
What's wrong? Calm down.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.770
Don't think about having a no-no game, Goro.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:19.680
Ball!

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.020
Come on...

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:25.940
Six consecutive balls since the last batter?

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.730
What's he waiting for?

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:32.120
He'll have to be switched out at this rate.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:36.990
Damn...

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:38.710
What's wrong with me?

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:42.010
My shoulder's fine, but...

00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:44.890
I can't control my pitches at all.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:47.310
Ball!

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:48.840
Ball three!

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:56.510
Ball!

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:57.410
Ball four!

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:03.430
Bases loaded from an error and two walks?

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:05.650
Forget the no-no game...

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:07.270
Crap...

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:10.360
I screwed up his rhythm with my error.

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:17.650
What's wrong with me?

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:23.350
Am I unconsciously focusing too much on not giving any hits?

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:24.440
No...

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:26.160
That can't be it.

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:28.130
It must be something else...

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:34.130
Today's the only chance Goro has for a no-hitter debut in the majors.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.870
The dugout must be reluctant to switch him out.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:38.710
It appears he'll continue.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.330
Call the dugout.

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:48.480
Pardon?

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:54.140
I told him that we're switching if his next pitch isn't a strike.

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:59.220
Even though he's pitched a no-no game so far, he's probably tired from pitching the whole game.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.020
It's unfortunate, but he'll have to come off.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.420
But I just received a call from the owner.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:04.160
What?

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:08.880
Now hitting: number 34, Sireed!

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:12.800
I never thought he'd break down so easily.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:17.180
It's a shame to let the no-no go, but winning is more important.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:21.540
The first pitch right after two consecutive walks is bound to come in easy.

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:26.600
I'd rather have it be a ball than have it hit to the stands.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.620
One out and bases loaded!

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:32.950
With one hit, the game could be tied, or even turned around!

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:35.240
Let's hope Shigeno pulls through this bind.

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:37.200
H-Honda...

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:43.120
If he can get through this hopeless situation, he'll still have a chance for a no-hitter.

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:52.380
Shoot.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.130
Don't throw a strike!

00:17:58.480 --> 00:17:58.800
Out!

00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:05.560
Safe!

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.300
That was close...

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:10.500
He went back because the fly was shallow, but...

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:12.480
Well, it's two outs with the bases loaded.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:17.150
It's still a no-hitter, but the next batter is...

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:21.850
Now hitting: number 51,

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:24.490
Kyoshiro!

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:29.960
He's the last guy this inning!

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:31.840
Don't lose, Goro!

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:35.430
What's wrong?

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:36.670
What's wrong, rookie?

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:38.590
You've come this far, so go all the way!

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:39.260
That's right!

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:41.060
A no-hitter!

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:51.610
No-no! No-no! No-no!

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:50.600
Hey, Shigeno!

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.610
You all right?

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.650
Get it together, rookie!

00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:58.340
Even if Goro was obsessed with getting a no-no,

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:01.070
he wouldn't lose this much composure.

00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:04.990
It doesn't look like he's exhausted either.

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:08.250
It happened after a runner got on base from an error.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.410
No...

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.710
Foul! Foul!

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:16.800
That's when it started!

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:20.130
When Dean hit that wide foul.

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:31.980
Could Goro be...

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.720
C-Coach.

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:35.130
We shouldn't let this...

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:39.360
But if it's the owner's orders...

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:40.630
Don't switch him out.

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:43.280
We still have a chance for a no-no!

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:46.270
It may even go down in history!

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:49.160
I don't give a damn if we lose!

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.330
I'll fire you if you take him out!

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.650
Oh, they're not switching?

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:55.510
He's going to give up a hit.

00:19:56.950 --> 00:20:02.850
Sireed hit a poor fly, but that pitch could've easily been a home run.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:07.200
And now, he threw a short bouncing pitch even Keene couldn't catch.

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:12.100
If that's precisely the reason he's in this pinch,

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:16.520
they need to switch Goro out instead of being fixated on a no-no.

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:28.490
What the...

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:33.220
My body... feels like it's made out of lead.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.560
Hey, what are you just standing there for?

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:53.230
Are you scared now?

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:56.660
Time out!

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:57.730
Time!

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:03.800
What are you thinking?

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:11.730
This won't pass.

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:14.930
The dugout won't switch you out until you take a hit.

00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:18.210
Leave the mound yourself.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.880
Wh-What?

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:21.690
Why wouldn't you?

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:24.400
You can't pitch any strikes, and you can't even throw into my mitt.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:28.340
Not to mention you were spacing out on the mound just now.

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:33.310
Were you doing an image training of giving up a hit to Kyoshiro?

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:36.880
I'm not criticizing you.

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:40.540
You did more than enough as a starting pitcher.

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:45.240
If it weren't for the no-no, you would've been off the mound long ago.

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:47.590
So leave.

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:49.780
If you aren't obsessed with getting a no-no,

00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:52.660
we can win this game with Watts.

00:21:53.130 --> 00:21:54.600
What's Keene doing?

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:56.460
What's he saying to him?

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:05.590
Okay.

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:20.360
Wh-What is this?

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:22.940
Shigeno's leaving the mound!

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:32.200
Wh-What?!

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:59.140
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:59.140
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:04.520
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:04.520
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:10.780
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:10.780
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:15.580
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:15.580
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:22.170
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:22.170
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:28.050
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:28.050
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:33.850
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:33.850
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:39.310
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:39.310
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:45.770
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:45.770
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:51.030
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:54.490
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:51.030 --> 00:23:54.490
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:56.950
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.490 --> 00:24:03.330
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:56.950 --> 00:24:03.330
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:07.170
sotto

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:07.170
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:15.350
Preview

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:15.350
Preview

00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:12.240
Wh-What the...?

00:24:12.240 --> 00:24:15.030
What's going on with my body?

00:24:15.030 --> 00:24:15.740
I know.

00:24:15.740 --> 00:24:16.750
I must be sick.

00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:18.790
I must have caught a cold!

00:24:18.790 --> 00:24:22.560
How can I call myself a professional if I can't even manage my health?

00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:25.030
Next time on Major: In an Impossible Dilemma.

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:29.810
Next Time

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:29.810
Next Time

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:29.830
In an Impossible Dilemma

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:29.830
In an Impossible Dilemma

00:24:25.880 --> 00:24:30.460
Run toward the stage of your dreams!
